From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the display color matrix applies in linear light

Viz applies a display color matrix to the root render pass in the
output's encoding. Domicile sets one for a night light on a display
driven in HDR, where the output is PQ: a matrix there would bend the
curve the panel decodes rather than warm the light. SkiaRenderer now
applies it in linear sRGB, as a gamma ramp on an SDR display does in
effect.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 components/viz/service/display/skia_renderer.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/skia_renderer.cc b/components/viz/service/display/skia_renderer.cc
index 3eb7c87..ea74645 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/skia_renderer.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/skia_renderer.cc
@@ -3125,8 +3125,12 @@ sk_sp<SkColorFilter> SkiaRenderer::GetContentColorFilter() {
       current_frame()->current_render_pass == current_frame()->root_render_pass;
 
   if (is_root && output_surface_->color_matrix() != SkM44()) {
+    // domicile: in linear light, so the matrix scales light whatever the
+    // output encodes. A night light on a display driven in HDR would
+    // otherwise bend the PQ curve the panel decodes.
     color_transform =
-        SkColorFilters::Matrix(ToColorMatrix(output_surface_->color_matrix()));
+        SkColorFilters::Matrix(ToColorMatrix(output_surface_->color_matrix()))
+            ->makeWithWorkingColorSpace(SkColorSpace::MakeSRGBLinear());
   }
 
   sk_sp<SkColorFilter> tint_transform = nullptr;
